<%- include("../partials/head") %>
<%- include("../partials/navbar") %>

      <main class="site-main hosting-page">
        <div class="hosting-layout">
          <nav class="hosting-sidebar" aria-label="Hosting guide sections">
            <p class="hosting-sidebar__title">Hosting guide</p>
            <ul class="hosting-sidebar__list">
              <li><a href="#hosting-top">Overview</a></li>
              <li><a href="#steam-hosting">Steam hosting</a></li>
              <li><a href="#direct-connect">Direct Connect</a></li>
              <li><a href="#dedicated-server">Dedicated server</a></li>
              <li><a href="#ports">Ports</a></li>
              <li><a href="#hosting-help">Troubleshooting</a></li>
            </ul>
          </nav>
          <div class="hosting-content">
        <section class="section-panel hosting-hero" id="hosting-top" aria-labelledby="hosting-title">
          <div class="hosting-hero__signal" aria-hidden="true">
            <span>CO_HOST // TWO ROUTES</span>
            <span>STEAM P2P // DEDICATED</span>
          </div>
          <p class="section-kicker">Hosting guide</p>
          <h1 id="hosting-title">Host through Steam, or run a dedicated server.</h1>
          <p class="hosting-hero__lead">
            Steam hosting runs your world from your own PC, and friends join through Steam.
            A dedicated server runs on a VPS or an always-on PC, and players connect to its address and port.
          </p>
          <div class="hosting-hero__actions">
            <a class="co-btn co-btn--primary" href="#steam-hosting">Steam hosting</a>
            <a class="co-btn co-btn--ghost" href="#direct-connect">Direct Connect</a>
            <a class="co-btn co-btn--ghost" href="#dedicated-server">Dedicated server</a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="hosting-callout section-panel" aria-label="The short version">
          <div class="hosting-callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
          <div>
            <p class="section-kicker">The short version</p>
            <h2>Steam hosting needs no router setup</h2>
            <p>
              Steam hosting needs Steam running and signed in. Players who join can see your internet address (IP),
              so only host for people you trust. A dedicated server works the same way: players connect to its address and port.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="hosting-section" id="steam-hosting" aria-labelledby="steam-hosting-title">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="section-kicker">Recommended for friends</p>
            <h2 id="steam-hosting-title">Steam hosting</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="hosting-grid hosting-grid--two">
            <article class="hosting-card">
              <header class="hosting-card__header">
                <span class="hosting-card__index">HOST // 01</span>
                <h3>Start a Steam world</h3>
              </header>
              <ol class="hosting-step-list">
                <li>Leave Vault 111 and reach the open world. Invites only work from there.</li>
                <li>Open <strong>Friends (Steam)</strong> in the server browser.</li>
                <li>Check <strong>Listed server name</strong> and <strong>Max players</strong> under <strong>Server settings</strong>. Friends see them.</li>
                <li>Optionally enter a <strong>Server password</strong>.</li>
                <li>Click <strong>Start Hosting</strong>. The lobby shows your <strong>Friend Code</strong>.</li>
                <li>Click <strong>Copy</strong>, or <strong>Invite Steam friends</strong>.</li>
                <li>When your friends are ready, click <strong>Enter world</strong>. <strong>Friends connected</strong> counts who has joined.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="hosting-card__note">
                <strong>Stop Hosting</strong> ends the lobby. By default only your Steam friends can join, so add people as friends first
                or in the Launcher's Server settings turn off <strong>Steam friends only</strong> and set a password.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="hosting-card">
              <header class="hosting-card__header">
                <span class="hosting-card__index">PLAYER // 02</span>
                <h3>Join a Steam world</h3>
              </header>
              <ol class="hosting-step-list">
                <li>Open <strong>Friends (Steam)</strong> in the server browser.</li>
                <li>Under <strong>Join</strong>, paste the host's <strong>Friend Code</strong>, or part of their Steam name.</li>
                <li>Enter the password if the host set one.</li>
                <li>Click <strong>Join</strong>.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="hosting-card__note">
                Leave the code empty to join a friend who is already hosting. Their world appears in the host list with its own <strong>Join</strong> button.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="hosting-screenshot section-panel" id="direct-connect" aria-labelledby="direct-connect-title">
          <div class="hosting-screenshot__copy">
            <p class="section-kicker">Dedicated servers</p>
            <h2 id="direct-connect-title">Join with Direct Connect</h2>
            <p>
              Use Direct Connect to join a dedicated server by its address. Open the <strong>Direct Connect</strong> tab
              in the server browser. <strong>Server Address</strong> starts at 127.0.0.1 and <strong>Port</strong> at 7777.
              Enter the host's IP or domain, its port, and the password if it has one, then click <strong>Connect</strong>.
              You can also paste <code>host:port</code> or <code>[IPv6]:port</code> into the address field.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure>
            <div class="hosting-screenshot__frame">
              <img
                src="/assets/images/server-browser-direct-connect.webp"
                alt="Commonwealth Online server browser showing the Direct Connect screen"
                loading="lazy"
                width="1985"
                height="922"
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption>Server browser → Direct Connect // address, port, password, Connect.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section class="hosting-section" id="dedicated-server" aria-labelledby="dedicated-server-title">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="section-kicker">Always-on server</p>
            <h2 id="dedicated-server-title">Run a dedicated server</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="hosting-grid hosting-grid--two">
            <article class="hosting-card">
              <header class="hosting-card__header">
                <span class="hosting-card__index">HOST // 03</span>
                <h3>Start it from the Launcher</h3>
              </header>
              <ol class="hosting-step-list">
                <li>Open the Launcher and go to the <strong>Server</strong> page.</li>
                <li>Choose the <strong>DEDICATED</strong> tab. Steam P2P is the other tab.</li>
                <li>Read the warning. A dedicated server is meant for a VPS or a PC that is always on.</li>
                <li>In Settings, set the game port. It defaults to 7777.</li>
                <li>Start the server and give players your address and port.</li>
              </ol>
            </article>

            <article class="hosting-card">
              <header class="hosting-card__header">
                <span class="hosting-card__index">PLAYER // 04</span>
                <h3>Connect to it</h3>
              </header>
              <ol class="hosting-step-list">
                <li>Open the server browser and go to <strong>Direct Connect</strong>.</li>
                <li>Enter the server's IP or domain as <strong>Server Address</strong>.</li>
                <li>Enter the port the host gave you, then the password if there is one.</li>
                <li>Click <strong>Connect</strong>.</li>
              </ol>
              <p class="hosting-card__note">
                Servers on your own network also appear in the <strong>Friends (Steam)</strong> tab, under the LAN list.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="hosting-section" id="ports" aria-labelledby="ports-title">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="section-kicker">Network</p>
            <h2 id="ports-title">Ports for a dedicated server</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="hosting-grid hosting-grid--two">
            <article class="hosting-card hosting-card--compact">
              <header class="hosting-card__header">
                <span class="hosting-card__index">GAME // UDP</span>
                <h3>Game port: 7777</h3>
              </header>
              <p>
                Players connect on UDP <code>7777</code> by default. Forward it on your router and allow it through the
                firewall to let players in from outside your network.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="hosting-card hosting-card--compact">
              <header class="hosting-card__header">
                <span class="hosting-card__index">LAN // UDP</span>
                <h3>LAN discovery: 7778</h3>
              </header>
              <p>
                LAN discovery uses UDP <code>7778</code> so the server shows up for players on the same network.
                You can change the port or turn <strong>LAN discovery</strong> off in the server settings.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <div class="hosting-firewall">
            <strong>Keep the admin port closed</strong>
            <span>The admin port listens on TCP <code>127.0.0.1:7779</code> only. Do not forward it.</span>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="hosting-section" id="hosting-help" aria-labelledby="hosting-help-title">
          <div class="section-head">
            <p class="section-kicker">Signal repair</p>
            <h2 id="hosting-help-title">Quick troubleshooting</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="hosting-troubleshooting">
            <details open>
              <summary>Invite Steam friends does nothing</summary>
              <p>Invites only work in the open world. Leave Vault 111, then invite again.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>"This host only lets their Steam friends join."</summary>
              <p>Add the player as a Steam friend. Or, in the Launcher's Server settings, turn off <strong>Steam friends only</strong> and set a server password so anyone with the password can join.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>The Friend Code is rejected</summary>
              <p>Use the code from the host's lobby, or part of their Steam name. A Friend Code is a number from the host's Steam profile.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>Locked out after wrong passwords</summary>
              <p>After five wrong passwords, that Steam account is locked out for five minutes. Wait, then try again with the right password.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>The server directory is unavailable</summary>
              <p>Join with <strong>Direct Connect</strong> instead, using the server's address and port.</p>
            </details>
            <details>
              <summary>LAN servers don't appear</summary>
              <p>Both PCs must be on the same network. The host must have LAN discovery on, and UDP <code>7778</code> must be allowed through its firewall.</p>
            </details>
          </div>
        </section>
          </div>
        </div>
      </main>

